v B-\frac{\sigma}{3 \epsilon_{0}}=\rho \frac{d \sigma}{d t}
\end{gathered}
\tag{44}
$$

As the magnetic field is uniform to calculate force path of the current will not matter. Hence assuming it to be straight line between two points located at $\theta$ and $-\theta$. So the force can be written as -

$$
\begin{gathered}
d F=B \times d I \times l \\
