$$
C=\frac{1}{v} \frac{\delta Q}{d T}=C_{V}+\frac{p}{v} \frac{d V}{d T}
\tag{B.2}
$$

Here $C_{V}$ stands for the molar heat capacity of the gas at constant volume, $p$ designates its pressure, $v$ is the total amount of moles of gas in the bubble, $V$ and $T$ denote the volume and temperature of the gas, respectively.

Evaluate the derivative standing on the right hand side of (B.2). According to the Laplace formula, the gas pressure inside the bubble is defined by

