p^{3} V=\text { const. }
\tag{B.4}
$$

The equation of state of an ideal gas has the form

$$
p V=v R T
\tag{B.5}
$$

and hence equation (B.4) can be rewritten as

$$
T^{3} V^{-2}=\text { const. }
\tag{B.6}
